+# Agent Note: Recovery of retained tool outcomes
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-13-retained-tool-outcomes.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A tool can persist a result before its receipt reaches the Session log. Crash repair correctly reports an unknown outcome, but a consumer with retained evidence then needs to deliver the actual result. Content-only replacement cannot change that error flag.
+
+## Decision
+
+A tool-result replacement may correct an error to success when it cites the failed receipt and at least one earlier retained event. Message ID, call ID, source, turn, step and other metadata remain unchanged. The replacement removes error identity and changes only the result content and error flag. Consumers validate their own retained outcomes before appending the replacement. The surface validates identities and references; it does not interpret external application state.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Keeping isError true misrepresents a known successful outcome. Reexecuting the tool can repeat effects. Appending an unrelated success produces duplicate results for the same call. Mutating the old event destroys request reconstruction. An entirely separate recovery message type would duplicate the existing replacement and provenance mechanisms.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The original error remains in history, while future requests use the corrected surface node. Success-to-error rewrites and identity changes remain invalid. Tests cover required evidence, stable identity and historical retention. No event fields, Session version, Loop phase or SDK wire type changes.
